Cold-restore a dead agent pane on a headless host

After a workspace restart, opening an agent pane in the tile renders its full
transcript in chat view while typing in the composer lands in a shell:
`bash: command not found`. Native chat is a TUI wrapper that writes bytes into
the pane's PTY, so a pane backed by a plain shell shows real history beside a
composer talking to bash. Desktop rebuilds the resume in its renderer; `orca
serve` has no renderer, so the materialize path launched a fresh agent at best.

`resolveHeadlessAgentColdRestore` reads the host's own agent-hook rows - which
are hydrated from disk at startup and carry `agentType` plus `providerSession` -
by pane key, and the materialize path resumes through upstream's
`buildAgentResumeStartupPlan` so both variants share one platform and shell
resolution. A non-resumable agent or an unusable session id falls back to a
fresh launch rather than failing the tab open.

To test, restart the workspace, open an agent pane in the tile and continue the
conversation: the agent should answer with full prior context and run shell
commands. Covered by `headless-agent-cold-restore.test.ts`.

